    <section class="rise-fall" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1200 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">The Olmec centre of San Lorenzo flourishes on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-coast-of-mexico">Gulf Coast of Mexico</a>, with the earliest monumental religious art of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesoamerica">Mesoamerica</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 200</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyramid-of-the-sun">Pyramid of the Sun</a> is completed at Teotihuacan, the city the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztecs</a> later believed to be the birthplace of the sun</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">292</span><span class="rf-text">Stela 29 is raised at Tikal, the earliest known dated monument of the Maya lowlands</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1325</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> found <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>, by tradition where their god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huitzilopochtli">Huitzilopochtli</a> had promised</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1487</span><span class="rf-text">The Great Temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> is rededicated with the sacrifice of many captives</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1521</span><span class="rf-text">The fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> to the Spanish and their allies ends the Aztec state religion</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1562</span><span class="rf-text">The friar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-landa">Diego de Landa</a> burns Maya books and images at Maní in Yucatán</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1697</span><span class="rf-text">The Spanish take Nojpetén, capital of the Itza, the last independent Maya kingdom</span></li></ol>
    </section>

